><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250604102941+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250604103000+10'00'" name="d7c8622e-879d-4df0-b68a-79f15e0280d7" page="1" coords="51.000015,197.624649,204.092285,197.624649,51.000015,186.824677,204.092285,186.824677,42.000015,186.626633,204.099838,186.626633,42.000015,175.826660,204.099838,175.826660,42.000015,175.628647,204.103470,175.628647,42.000015,164.828674,204.103470,164.828674,42.000015,164.630630,204.092758,164.630630,42.000015,153.830658,204.092758,153.830658,42.000015,153.632645,204.112442,153.632645,42.000015,142.832672,204.112442,142.832672,42.000015,142.634628,204.097260,142.634628,42.000015,131.834656,204.097260,131.834656,42.000015,131.636627,204.097000,131.636627,42.000015,120.836655,204.097000,120.836655,42.000015,120.638626,204.092636,120.638626,42.000015,109.838654,204.092636,109.838654,42.000015,109.640625,206.601059,109.640625,42.000015,98.840652,206.601059,98.840652,42.000015,98.642624,204.095428,98.642624,42.000015,87.842651,204.095428,87.842651,42.000015,87.644623,204.098755,87.644623,42.000015,76.844650,204.098755,76.844650,42.000015,76.646622,114.305847,76.646622,42.000015,65.846649,114.305847,65.846649" rect="41.662506,65.509140,206.938568,197.962158" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c:</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
> We determined that the diagnostic&#xD;utility of clinical examination and diagnostic&#xD;imaging in isolation are limited and&#xD;recommend a comprehensive diagnostic&#xD;approach of patient symptoms, clinical&#xD;signs and diagnostic imaging. We recognise&#xD;that the diagnostic capability of matching&#xD;symptoms, clinical signs and diagnostic&#xD;imaging is unknown for patients with hip-related&#xD;pain and recommend that future&#xD;studies be considered in determining such&#xD;diagnostic utilities.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
